# 13 — Agent Ergonomics

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/thinking-06-agent-ergonomics` first: it's the case for this phase (the agent building an old temple room in `mariobros`, what cost tokens and what went unchecked), and its ideas are numbered there as they're referred to here (T1–T10). Then `plans/10-array-tools` §3 and §9 (arrays, layouts, following, `arrayLayout`), `plans/09-review-loop` (`render_view`, the `review` topic) and `plans/thinking-04-evals` (measuring the tool). This phase is almost all MCP surface: it makes the agent's tools **cheaper** (fewer tokens, fewer calls) and lets it **check sightlines** with a tool instead of a render or an assertion. It adds:
> - **compact results** and **where array items are:** results stop echoing points, and say where each item stands and how high its top is (T3, T1, T10);
> - **arcs and spirals** for lines and path layouts, and a **rising circle** (T2);
> - **one batch, one call:** references between the shapes of one `draw_shapes`, groups made in the same batch, and **defining an entity** without drawing it in the scene (T7, T8);
> - **surfaces:** a node's walking surface as one shared function, so things can **stand on** other things and lines can go **through** nodes, as jump arcs, live (T9, T1);
> - **`check_sight`:** what's visible from a point, and what blocks it, in text (T5);
> - **renders that see inside:** hiding nodes and clipping above a height, for one render (T6);
> - **the eval run again:** the temple prompt, before and after, counted (thinking-04).
>
> Checking jumps against the game's numbers (T4: the facts as data, `check_route`) is deliberately **not** in this phase (§2, Out).
>
> The work is split into small increments (§10). Each ends with the human ↔ agent loop working, `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` passing, a scripted check against a spare server (`PORT=5171 DATA_DIR=<scratch>`), and, where the editor changes, a browser checklist for Orlando. The server's MCP version goes up one patch per increment, from 0.0.23: restart the server and reconnect with `/mcp` after each. Add this phase's terms to `GLOSSARY.md` (marked "from 13") as they land. Log progress in §13 at the end of this file.

